FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: permit-application.

OFF THE RECORD: Form 91-B, Application for a Permit to Apply for a
OFF THE RECORD: Permit. The applicant is served two summonses: one for
OFF THE RECORD: a name, one for an age. Deficient applications are
OFF THE RECORD: held in contempt, which is faster than rejecting them.

HEREINAFTER, minimum-age SHALL MEAN 18.
HEREINAFTER, maximum-age SHALL MEAN 65.

ARTICLE 1.
    AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER applicant.
    AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER stated-age.

ARTICLE 2.
    OFF THE RECORD: ages arrive as integers or as strings, depending on
    OFF THE RECORD: how the clerk was feeling. THE SUM CERTAIN accepts both.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT age IS THE SUM CERTAIN OF stated-age.
    SHOULD THE LENGTH OF applicant FALL SHORT OF 2,
        HOLD "an applicant of insufficient length" IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD age FALL SHORT OF minimum-age OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE age EXCEED maximum-age,
        HOLD applicant PLUS " (aged " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF age
            PLUS ") is not of permissible age" IN CONTEMPT.

ARTICLE 3.
    PROCLAIM "Application received from " PLUS applicant PLUS ".".
    PROCLAIM "It will be processed in due course.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
